- Story & Context: Sapan-Diem sits on his porch, listening to the static between radio frequencies and confessing to the river that he is the one who hid the mail because he feared the news would change his sister's heart. The Juno-60 sweeps through a thick, detuned chorus that sounds like a confession blurring in the humidity, as he murmurs, "why speak when the current carries the doubt for us?"
